<title>UK: European jet falls again with gas oil futures.</title>
<headline>European jet falls again with gas oil futures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE jet fell again on Friday, pressured by weaker IPE gas oil and lacklustre premiums.</p>
<p>March IPE gas oil closed $2 a tonne lower at $162.50.</p>
<p>Traders said activity was still slow, although some dealers thought the weaker numbers might attract some buying. Talk on jet barges put premiums around March IPE gas oil +$21-22 fob ARA with cargoes a couple of dollars stronger on a cif basis.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
